bibliograph (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Resolve shelving rows whose edition is missing from the catalog instead of
    dropping them. `catalogEditionUriFromRkey` also maps `isbndb.*` rkeys now:
    without that mapping a record whose `book.ref` was absent (every record the
    app writes) could not be tied to its edition URI at all, so 1593 shelving
    rows were unresolvable even once the catalog held them.
  * Shelf hydration now asks the provider that owns an edition's rkey prefix
    (OpenLibrary, Google Books, ISBNdb) when the row is absent, persists the
    result through the normal ingest path, and re-hydrates for the same
    response. Bounded to 6 editions per request with a 2.5 s budget, and misses
    are remembered for 10 minutes so a page of unresolvable rows does not retry
    them on every call.
  * Add `mise`/`pnpm run backfill:shelving-editions`: scans shelving records for
    editions the catalog lacks and fills them from their provider, or from
    another catalog database (`--copy-from`) when one is available.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bibliograph (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the PDS fallback shared by listShelves, listShelvesWithBooks and
    listBooksOnShelf. The listRecords parser validated a record's `value` with
    the lexicon-record builder, which requires an object schema carrying a
    literal `$type`, and read the result as `success`/`output` instead of
    `ok`/`value`. Either mistake throws, and the handler's catch turned that
    into an empty result, so these queries answered only from the tap cache:
    listShelves returned {"shelves":[]} for a repo whose PDS held four shelf
    records, and shelf pages reported "shelf not found" for shelves that
    existed.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bibliograph (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship bibliograph-jobs.service, the unit that runs the Graphile Worker task
    lists in src/worker-search-jobs.ts. Without it the queued
    tap-record-upsert-batch jobs are never executed, so `records` never fills
    and every getReviewsByBook answer is empty. Enabled and started by
    dh_installsystemd like the other long-running units.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Wed, 29 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bibliograph (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add logging/metrics for empty contributor names in searchEditions
    (xrpc-router.ts, metrics.ts: invalidContributorResponsesTotal) and
    getRecord (book-contributor-view.ts) responses.

